az account show --output table

To solve login issues,
az account clear                                        
az config set core.enable_broker_on_windows=false
az login --tenant <tenant-id> 

Choose your Image Details(Ex: ubuntu),
az vm image list-publishers --location eastus --output table|grep -i canonical
az vm image list-offers --location eastus --publisher Canonical --output table
az vm image list-skus --location eastus \
   --publisher Canonical --offer 0001-com-ubuntu-server-jammy \
   --output table

Verify vm-sizes in the region,
az vm list-sizes \
  --location eastus \
  --output table | grep Standard_D
Note: Always verify SKUs in the portal and use them!

Backend setup,
az storage account create -n pocstorageaccount1013 -g supero-rg -l eastus --sku Standard_LRS --kind StorageV2
az storage container create -n terraformstate --account-name pocstorageaccount1013 --auth-mode login